stack by series. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" defines\nseries; a discrete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"},{"type":"text","value":" channel may infer it when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout: stack(options)"},{"type":"text","value":" for explicit order, reversal, normalization,\ncentering, or wiggle offset. Supplying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y1"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2"},{"type":"text","value":" opts out and preserves\nauthored interval boundaries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"order: 'inside-out'"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offset: 'wiggle'"},{"type":"text","value":" for nonnegative\nstreamgraphs. Inside-out order follows series peaks and totals. The completed\nwiggle stack is translated once so the global minimum start is zero; individual\npositions are not rebased. Positions and series retain first-seen order, and a\nmissing position/series pair contributes zero to layout without emitting a\nsynthetic point."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input order and null-gap behavior match the line marks. Each valid row emits\none point at the upper "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" value, not at the lower baseline."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"areax","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaX"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaX"},{"type":"text","value":" is the transposed interval area: it fills between left and right\nnumeric x values along y."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const mark = areaX(rows, {\n  y: 'category',\n  x1: 'minimum',\n  x2: 'maximum',\n  z: 'series',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"function areaX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: AreaXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, InferredY>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric datum"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer thickness; implicitly stacked at each y"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implicit stack start"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit left boundary"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implicit stack end"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit right boundary; takes precedence over x"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row index"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared vertical position"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No explicit group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Area grouping; overrides color grouping"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Color-scale value; groups when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Top/nested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", y, then index"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable interaction identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Final paint, evaluated from the group's first row"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fill opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel<TDatum, string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional boundary stroke"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Boundary stroke width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"curve"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AreaXCurve"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Straight segments"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional transposed path generator"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StackLayout"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implicit diverging stack"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configured stack order or offset"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly ChartMarkState[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus-driven presentation overrides"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without explicit endpoints, repeated y positions stack by series. Supplying\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"},{"type":"text","value":" opts out and preserves authored interval boundaries. Each valid\nrow emits one point at its right "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line and area paths have one paint value. When both channels are present,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" wins for grouping and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"},{"type":"text","value":" may supply a different semantic paint value.\nKeep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"color"},{"type":"text","value":" constant within each explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" group; the first row supplies\nthe path color."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"curves","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Curves"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line and area marks accept a small path-generation contract rather than\nbundling interpolation algorithms:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartCurve {\n  line(points: readonly (readonly [number, number])[]): string\n  area(\n    top: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n    bottom: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n  ): string\n}\n\ninterface AreaXCurve {\n  areaX(\n    right: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n    left: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n  ): string\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional adapters are available:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { d3AreaXCurve } from '@tanstack/charts/d3/area-x'\nimport { d3Curve } from '@tanstack/charts/d3/shape'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"They accept a supplied curve factory and return the corresponding TanStack\ncontract. Which granular D3 module to install and why these algorithms remain\ninjected is documented once in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"layering-area-and-line","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layering area and line"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Area marks do not automatically draw their upper line. Compose the layers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'value',\n      z: 'series',\n      fillOpacity: 0.16,\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'value',\n      z: 'series',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: xScale },\n    y: { scale: yScale },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use matching channels and scales when the two layers must align. Identity\ninference is evaluated independently for every interactive layer; supply a\nkey only where its automatic candidate is not stable."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"liney","text":"lineY","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"linex","text":"lineX","level":2},{"id":"areay","text":"areaY","level":2},{"id":"options-2","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"areax","text":"areaX","level":2},{"id":"options-3","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"curves","text":"Curves","level":2},{"id":"layering-area-and-line","text":"Layering area and line","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLine and area marks consume an iterable directly. Channels may be compatible\nfield names or accessors. Rows whose required positional value is null,\nundefined, invalid, or nonfinite create gaps instead of connecting across\nmissing data.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  areaX,\n  areaY,\n  defineChart,\n  lineX,\n  lineY,\n  stack,\n} from '@tanstack/charts'\n```\n\n## `lineY`\n\n`lineY` connects consecutive valid rows within each path group. An explicit\n`z` defines the groups. When `z` is omitted and `color` is present, `color`\ndefines them.\n\n```ts\nconst mark = lineY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  points: true,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction lineY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: LineYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, number>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option            | Type                            | Default                        | Meaning                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`              | `string`                        | Layer-derived                  | Stable mark ID                                 |\n| `x`               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`  | Row index                      | Horizontal value                               |\n| `y`               | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`      | Numeric datum                  | Vertical value                                 |\n| `z`               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`    | No explicit group              | Path grouping; overrides color grouping        |\n| `color`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`    | `z`                            | Color-scale value; groups when `z` is absent   |\n| `key`             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`     | Top/nested `id`, x, then index | Stable interaction and scene identity          |\n| `stroke`          | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>` | Resolved color                 | Final path paint; evaluated from the first row |\n| `strokeOpacity`   | `number`                        | SVG default                    | Stroke opacity                                 |\n| `strokeWidth`     | `number`                        | `2.25`                         | Stroke width                                   |\n| `strokeDasharray` | `string`                        | None                           | SVG dash array                                 |\n| `lineCap`         | `SceneStyle[\"lineCap\"]`         | `\"round\"`                      | Stroke endpoint shape                          |\n| `lineJoin`        | `SceneStyle[\"lineJoin\"]`        | `\"round\"`                      | Stroke corner shape                            |\n| `points`          | `boolean`                       | `false`                        | Draws a radius-`2.5` dot at each valid point   |\n| `curve`           | `ChartCurve`                    | Straight segments              | Optional path generator                        |\n| `states`          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`     | None                           | Focus-driven presentation overrides            |\n\nInput order is path order. Sort rows before creating the mark when semantic x\norder differs from input order. A null row flushes the current segment; later\nvalid rows begin a new segment in the same group.\n\nEach valid row emits one interaction point at its scaled x/y coordinate.\n`groupLabel` is the string form of the effective path group, or the mark ID\nwithout a group.\n\n## `lineX`\n\n`lineX` is the transposed line mark. It connects numeric x values along a\nnumeric, categorical, or temporal y channel:\n\n```ts\nconst mark = lineX(rows, {\n  x: 'value',\n  y: 'category',\n  z: 'series',\n  points: true,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction lineX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: LineXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, InferredY>\n```\n\nIts options transpose `lineY`: `x` is the numeric value channel and defaults\nto a numeric datum; `y` is the longitudinal `ChartValue` channel and defaults\nto row index. Identity falls back to y, invalid rows create segment gaps, and\ninput order remains path order. Grouping, paint, points, curves, states, and\nmotion use the same contract. Line interaction follows y affinity so keyboard\nand pointer traversal match the longitudinal axis.\n\n`lineX` inherits these stroke-shape options from the shared line contract:\n\n| Option     | Type                     | Default   | Meaning               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | --------- | --------------------- |\n| `lineCap`  | `SceneStyle[\"lineCap\"]`  | `\"round\"` | Stroke endpoint shape |\n| `lineJoin` | `SceneStyle[\"lineJoin\"]` | `\"round\"` | Stroke corner shape   |\n\n## `areaY`\n\n`areaY` fills between a numeric upper channel and a numeric lower baseline\nalong x.\n\n```ts\nconst mark = areaY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y1: 'low',\n  y2: 'high',\n  z: 'series',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction areaY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: AreaYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, number>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option        | Type                                 | Default                        | Meaning                                                        |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`          | `string`                             | Layer-derived                  | Stable mark ID                                                 |\n| `x`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Row index                      | Shared horizontal position                                     |\n| `y`           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`           | Numeric datum                  | Layer thickness; implicitly stacked at each x                  |\n| `y1`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack start           | Explicit lower boundary                                        |\n| `y2`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack end             | Explicit upper boundary; takes precedence over y               |\n| `z`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | No explicit group              | Area grouping; overrides color grouping                        |\n| `color`       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | `z`                            | Color-scale value; groups when `z` is absent                   |\n| `key`         | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`          | Top/nested `id`, x, then index | Stable interaction identity                                    |\n| `fill`        | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | Resolved color                 | Final area paint; evaluated from the group's first row         |\n| `fillOpacity` | `number`                             | `0.2`                          | Fill opacity                                                   |\n| `stroke`      | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | None                           | Optional boundary stroke, evaluated from the group's first row |\n| `strokeWidth` | `number`                             | SVG default                    | Boundary stroke width                                          |\n| `curve`       | `ChartCurve`                         | Straight segments              | Optional path generator                                        |\n| `layout`      | `StackLayout`                        | Implicit diverging stack       | Configured stack order or offset                               |\n| `states`      | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`          | None                           | Focus-driven presentation overrides                            |\n\nWithout explicit endpoints, repeated x positions stack by series. `z` defines\nseries; a discrete `color` channel may infer it when `z` is absent. Use\n`layout: stack(options)` for explicit order, reversal, normalization,\ncentering, or wiggle offset. Supplying `y1` or `y2` opts out and preserves\nauthored interval boundaries.\n\nUse `order: 'inside-out'` with `offset: 'wiggle'` for nonnegative\nstreamgraphs. Inside-out order follows series peaks and totals. The completed\nwiggle stack is translated once so the global minimum start is zero; individual\npositions are not rebased. Positions and series retain first-seen order, and a\nmissing position/series pair contributes zero to layout without emitting a\nsynthetic point.\n\nInput order and null-gap behavior match the line marks. Each valid row emits\none point at the upper `y2`/`y` value, not at the lower baseline.\n\n## `areaX`\n\n`areaX` is the transposed interval area: it fills between left and right\nnumeric x values along y.\n\n```ts\nconst mark = areaX(rows, {\n  y: 'category',\n  x1: 'minimum',\n  x2: 'maximum',\n  z: 'series',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction areaX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: AreaXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, InferredY>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option        | Type                                 | Default                        | Meaning                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`          | `string`                             | Layer-derived                  | Stable mark ID                                    |\n| `x`           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`           | Numeric datum                  | Layer thickness; implicitly stacked at each y     |\n| `x1`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack start           | Explicit left boundary                            |\n| `x2`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack end             | Explicit right boundary; takes precedence over x  |\n| `y`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Row index                      | Shared vertical position                          |\n| `z`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | No explicit group              | Area grouping; overrides color grouping           |\n| `color`       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | `z`                            | Color-scale value; groups when `z` is absent      |\n| `key`         | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`          | Top/nested `id`, y, then index | Stable interaction identity                       |\n| `fill`        | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | Resolved color                 | Final paint, evaluated from the group's first row |\n| `fillOpacity` | `number`                             | `0.2`                          | Fill opacity                                      |\n| `stroke`      | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | None                           | Optional boundary stroke                          |\n| `strokeWidth` | `number`                             | SVG default                    | Boundary stroke width                             |\n| `curve`       | `AreaXCurve`                         | Straight segments              | Optional transposed path generator                |\n| `layout`      | `StackLayout`                        | Implicit diverging stack       | Configured stack order or offset                  |\n| `states`      | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`          | None                           | Focus-driven presentation overrides               |\n\nWithout explicit endpoints, repeated y positions stack by series. Supplying\n`x1` or `x2` opts out and preserves authored interval boundaries. Each valid\nrow emits one point at its right `x2`/`x` value.\n\nLine and area paths have one paint value. When both channels are present,\n`z` wins for grouping and `color` may supply a different semantic paint value.\nKeep `color` constant within each explicit `z` group; the first row supplies\nthe path color.\n\n## Curves\n\nLine and area marks accept a small path-generation contract rather than\nbundling interpolation algorithms:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartCurve {\n  line(points: readonly (readonly [number, number])[]): string\n  area(\n    top: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n    bottom: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n  ): string\n}\n\ninterface AreaXCurve {\n  areaX(\n    right: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n    left: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n  ): string\n}\n```\n\nOptional adapters are available:\n\n```ts\nimport { d3AreaXCurve } from '@tanstack/charts/d3/area-x'\nimport { d3Curve } from '@tanstack/charts/d3/shape'\n```\n\nThey accept a supplied curve factory and return the corresponding TanStack\ncontract. Which granular D3 module to install and why these algorithms remain\ninjected is documented once in\n[Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md).\n\n## Layering area and line\n\nArea marks do not automatically draw their upper line. Compose the layers:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'value',\n      z: 'series',\n      fillOpacity: 0.16,\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'value',\n      z: 'series',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: xScale },\n    y: { scale: yScale },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUse matching channels and scales when the two layers must align. Identity\ninference is evaluated independently for every interactive layer; supply a\nkey only where its automatic candidate is not stable.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Line and Area Marks\ndescription: Reference for lineY, lineX, areaY, areaX, grouping, null gaps, interval baselines, points, and optional curve bridges.\n---\n\nLine and area marks consume an iterable directly. Channels may be compatible\nfield names or accessors. Rows whose required positional value is null,\nundefined, invalid, or nonfinite create gaps instead of connecting across\nmissing data.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  areaX,\n  areaY,\n  defineChart,\n  lineX,\n  lineY,\n  stack,\n} from '@tanstack/charts'\n```\n\n## `lineY`\n\n`lineY` connects consecutive valid rows within each path group. An explicit\n`z` defines the groups. When `z` is omitted and `color` is present, `color`\ndefines them.\n\n```ts\nconst mark = lineY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  points: true,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction lineY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: LineYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, number>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option            | Type                            | Default                        | Meaning                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`              | `string`                        | Layer-derived                  | Stable mark ID                                 |\n| `x`               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`  | Row index                      | Horizontal value                               |\n| `y`               | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`      | Numeric datum                  | Vertical value                                 |\n| `z`               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`    | No explicit group              | Path grouping; overrides color grouping        |\n| `color`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`    | `z`                            | Color-scale value; groups when `z` is absent   |\n| `key`             | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`     | Top/nested `id`, x, then index | Stable interaction and scene identity          |\n| `stroke`          | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>` | Resolved color                 | Final path paint; evaluated from the first row |\n| `strokeOpacity`   | `number`                        | SVG default                    | Stroke opacity                                 |\n| `strokeWidth`     | `number`                        | `2.25`                         | Stroke width                                   |\n| `strokeDasharray` | `string`                        | None                           | SVG dash array                                 |\n| `lineCap`         | `SceneStyle[\"lineCap\"]`         | `\"round\"`                      | Stroke endpoint shape                          |\n| `lineJoin`        | `SceneStyle[\"lineJoin\"]`        | `\"round\"`                      | Stroke corner shape                            |\n| `points`          | `boolean`                       | `false`                        | Draws a radius-`2.5` dot at each valid point   |\n| `curve`           | `ChartCurve`                    | Straight segments              | Optional path generator                        |\n| `states`          | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`     | None                           | Focus-driven presentation overrides            |\n\nInput order is path order. Sort rows before creating the mark when semantic x\norder differs from input order. A null row flushes the current segment; later\nvalid rows begin a new segment in the same group.\n\nEach valid row emits one interaction point at its scaled x/y coordinate.\n`groupLabel` is the string form of the effective path group, or the mark ID\nwithout a group.\n\n## `lineX`\n\n`lineX` is the transposed line mark. It connects numeric x values along a\nnumeric, categorical, or temporal y channel:\n\n```ts\nconst mark = lineX(rows, {\n  x: 'value',\n  y: 'category',\n  z: 'series',\n  points: true,\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction lineX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: LineXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, InferredY>\n```\n\nIts options transpose `lineY`: `x` is the numeric value channel and defaults\nto a numeric datum; `y` is the longitudinal `ChartValue` channel and defaults\nto row index. Identity falls back to y, invalid rows create segment gaps, and\ninput order remains path order. Grouping, paint, points, curves, states, and\nmotion use the same contract. Line interaction follows y affinity so keyboard\nand pointer traversal match the longitudinal axis.\n\n`lineX` inherits these stroke-shape options from the shared line contract:\n\n| Option     | Type                     | Default   | Meaning               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | --------- | --------------------- |\n| `lineCap`  | `SceneStyle[\"lineCap\"]`  | `\"round\"` | Stroke endpoint shape |\n| `lineJoin` | `SceneStyle[\"lineJoin\"]` | `\"round\"` | Stroke corner shape   |\n\n## `areaY`\n\n`areaY` fills between a numeric upper channel and a numeric lower baseline\nalong x.\n\n```ts\nconst mark = areaY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y1: 'low',\n  y2: 'high',\n  z: 'series',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction areaY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: AreaYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, InferredX, number>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option        | Type                                 | Default                        | Meaning                                                        |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`          | `string`                             | Layer-derived                  | Stable mark ID                                                 |\n| `x`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Row index                      | Shared horizontal position                                     |\n| `y`           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`           | Numeric datum                  | Layer thickness; implicitly stacked at each x                  |\n| `y1`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack start           | Explicit lower boundary                                        |\n| `y2`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack end             | Explicit upper boundary; takes precedence over y               |\n| `z`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | No explicit group              | Area grouping; overrides color grouping                        |\n| `color`       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | `z`                            | Color-scale value; groups when `z` is absent                   |\n| `key`         | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`          | Top/nested `id`, x, then index | Stable interaction identity                                    |\n| `fill`        | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | Resolved color                 | Final area paint; evaluated from the group's first row         |\n| `fillOpacity` | `number`                             | `0.2`                          | Fill opacity                                                   |\n| `stroke`      | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | None                           | Optional boundary stroke, evaluated from the group's first row |\n| `strokeWidth` | `number`                             | SVG default                    | Boundary stroke width                                          |\n| `curve`       | `ChartCurve`                         | Straight segments              | Optional path generator                                        |\n| `layout`      | `StackLayout`                        | Implicit diverging stack       | Configured stack order or offset                               |\n| `states`      | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`          | None                           | Focus-driven presentation overrides                            |\n\nWithout explicit endpoints, repeated x positions stack by series. `z` defines\nseries; a discrete `color` channel may infer it when `z` is absent. Use\n`layout: stack(options)` for explicit order, reversal, normalization,\ncentering, or wiggle offset. Supplying `y1` or `y2` opts out and preserves\nauthored interval boundaries.\n\nUse `order: 'inside-out'` with `offset: 'wiggle'` for nonnegative\nstreamgraphs. Inside-out order follows series peaks and totals. The completed\nwiggle stack is translated once so the global minimum start is zero; individual\npositions are not rebased. Positions and series retain first-seen order, and a\nmissing position/series pair contributes zero to layout without emitting a\nsynthetic point.\n\nInput order and null-gap behavior match the line marks. Each valid row emits\none point at the upper `y2`/`y` value, not at the lower baseline.\n\n## `areaX`\n\n`areaX` is the transposed interval area: it fills between left and right\nnumeric x values along y.\n\n```ts\nconst mark = areaX(rows, {\n  y: 'category',\n  x1: 'minimum',\n  x2: 'maximum',\n  z: 'series',\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nfunction areaX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options?: AreaXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<TDatum, number, InferredY>\n```\n\n### Options\n\n| Option        | Type                                 | Default                        | Meaning                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`          | `string`                             | Layer-derived                  | Stable mark ID                                    |\n| `x`           | `Channel<TDatum, number?>`           | Numeric datum                  | Layer thickness; implicitly stacked at each y     |\n| `x1`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack start           | Explicit left boundary                            |\n| `x2`          | `number \\| Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Implicit stack end             | Explicit right boundary; takes precedence over x  |\n| `y`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`       | Row index                      | Shared vertical position                          |\n| `z`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | No explicit group              | Area grouping; overrides color grouping           |\n| `color`       | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`         | `z`                            | Color-scale value; groups when `z` is absent      |\n| `key`         | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`          | Top/nested `id`, y, then index | Stable interaction identity                       |\n| `fill`        | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | Resolved color                 | Final paint, evaluated from the group's first row |\n| `fillOpacity` | `number`                             | `0.2`                          | Fill opacity                                      |\n| `stroke`      | `VisualChannel<TDatum, string>`      | None                           | Optional boundary stroke                          |\n| `strokeWidth` | `number`                             | SVG default                    | Boundary stroke width                             |\n| `curve`       | `AreaXCurve`                         | Straight segments              | Optional transposed path generator                |\n| `layout`      | `StackLayout`                        | Implicit diverging stack       | Configured stack order or offset                  |\n| `states`      | `readonly ChartMarkState[]`          | None                           | Focus-driven presentation overrides               |\n\nWithout explicit endpoints, repeated y positions stack by series. Supplying\n`x1` or `x2` opts out and preserves authored interval boundaries. Each valid\nrow emits one point at its right `x2`/`x` value.\n\nLine and area paths have one paint value. When both channels are present,\n`z` wins for grouping and `color` may supply a different semantic paint value.\nKeep `color` constant within each explicit `z` group; the first row supplies\nthe path color.\n\n## Curves\n\nLine and area marks accept a small path-generation contract rather than\nbundling interpolation algorithms:\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartCurve {\n  line(points: readonly (readonly [number, number])[]): string\n  area(\n    top: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n    bottom: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n  ): string\n}\n\ninterface AreaXCurve {\n  areaX(\n    right: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n    left: readonly (readonly [number, number])[],\n  ): string\n}\n```\n\nOptional adapters are available:\n\n```ts\nimport { d3AreaXCurve } from '@tanstack/charts/d3/area-x'\nimport { d3Curve } from '@tanstack/charts/d3/shape'\n```\n\nThey accept a supplied curve factory and return the corresponding TanStack\ncontract. Which granular D3 module to install and why these algorithms remain\ninjected is documented once in\n[Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md).\n\n## Layering area and line\n\nArea marks do not automatically draw their upper line. Compose the layers:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    areaY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'value',\n      z: 'series',\n      fillOpacity: 0.16,\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'value',\n      z: 'series',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: xScale },\n    y: { scale: yScale },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUse matching channels and scales when the two layers must align. Identity\ninference is evaluated independently for every interactive layer; supply a\nkey only where its automatic candidate is not stable.\n"}
